Time-Space tradeoff 
    -- when you improve time complexity we use more space to significantly improve time complexity.

Trailing Zeros -- they come from 2 and 5s 
    Keep dividing by powers of 5 until the power exceeds n.
    and sum their answers, that will be the number of trailing zeros.

Euclidean Theorem 
    -- LCM(a, b) = [(a x b)/HCF(a,b)]

BIT MANULPATION:
    write their table and observations
    XOR -- if a array is give with consicutive numbers but one number is missing, eg 1^3^4^5, we XOR this with 1^2^3^4^5, to find 2 (only when one number is missing, does not work for multiple missing values)


